FYDE: ARM: dts: bcm2711: add ramoops/pstore region for Raspberry Pi 4

Same fix as the BCM2712/Pi 5 change, for the Pi 4 family (Pi 4B, Pi 400,
CM4). chromeos_startup's EncryptedRebootVault aborts with "pmsg0 not
enabled" because the BCM2711 device tree gives the ramoops (pstore-RAM)
backend no memory region, so /dev/pmsg0 is never created even though
CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM/PSTORE_PMSG are enabled.

Add a ramoops node under rmem. Base 0x0b000000 matches the stock RPi
ramoops overlay and lies in low System RAM (ZONE_DMA), clear of the
kernel image. pmsg-size is set explicitly because the driver defaults it
to 0 for a reserved-memory child (fs/pstore/ram.c).

This node is added in bcm2711.dtsi (not the shared bcm283x.dtsi) so it
applies only to the Pi 4 family, not the older 512MB-class boards. rmem
on bcm2711 is #address-cells=2 (override here) and #size-cells=1.

Index: v6.12-rpi/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711.dtsi
===================================================================
--- v6.12-rpi.orig/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711.dtsi
+++ v6.12-rpi/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711.dtsi
@@ -1105,6 +1105,23 @@
 
 &rmem {
 	#address-cells = <2>;
+
+	/*
+	 * pstore/ramoops region so crash logs and, crucially, the pmsg
+	 * buffer survive a reboot. chromeos_startup's EncryptedRebootVault
+	 * needs pstore-pmsg (/dev/pmsg0) to pass its encryption key across
+	 * reboots; without this node the ramoops backend gets no memory and
+	 * pmsg0 is never created. Base 0x0b000000 matches the stock RPi
+	 * ramoops overlay and sits in low System RAM (ZONE_DMA) clear of the
+	 * kernel image. rmem here is #address-cells=2, #size-cells=1.
+	 */
+	ramoops@b000000 {
+		compatible = "ramoops";
+		reg = <0x0 0x0b000000 0x100000>; /* 1 MB */
+		record-size = <0x20000>;  /* 128 KB */
+		console-size = <0x20000>; /* 128 KB */
+		pmsg-size = <0x20000>;    /* 128 KB */
+	};
 };
 
 &csi0 {
